# Template for the gitignored `.env` — the single local secrets file.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the DEV Supabase project's values (halcyon-dev).
#
# Who reads `.env`:
#   1. Docker Compose — interpolates ${...} in compose.yaml from it (Compose only
#      reads a file literally named `.env`), forwarding NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#      + SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY into the app container.
#   2. Next.js — its lowest-precedence env file; how the browser/SSR clients get
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY.
#
# What does NOT go here:
#   - DATABASE_URL / DIRECT_URL — never. Local Postgres URLs come from
#     compose.yaml (container) and .env.development (host `pnpm dev`).
#     Production URLs live only in Vercel env vars and CI secrets, so no local
#     file can point tooling at the production database.
#   - Production Supabase keys — production config lives in Vercel.
#
# All three vars are validated at server startup (src/lib/env.ts via
# src/instrumentation.ts); a missing value fails the boot with a clear error.

# Project URL and publishable key — safe to expose to the browser; RLS gates
# what the publishable key can do. Dashboard: halcyon-dev → Settings → API Keys.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://DEV_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_…

# Server-only secret key (bypasses RLS) — used by the admin client
# (deleteMyAccount) and the seed's demo-user creation. Never expose with a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Dashboard: halcyon-dev → Settings → API Keys → Secret keys.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_…
